cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite both the software and
  the underlying dataset.
title: >-
  Diminishing returns of electrode count, epoch duration, and model complexity
  in EEG brain-state classification
abstract: >-
  A reproducible pipeline measuring the marginal value of electrode count,
  recording window length, and model complexity for eyes-open versus
  eyes-closed classification from resting-state EEG, using the PhysioNet EEG
  Motor Movement/Imagery Dataset. All validation is participant-level, and the
  repository includes a deliberate epoch-level baseline that quantifies the
  inflation caused by that common error.
type: software
